      <h1>How MyHarmony drives a Harmony 600</h1>
      <p class=3D"lede">A teardown of the running Logitech MyHarmony 1.0.1.=
308 desktop app: what each layer does, which cloud services it calls, and t=
he USB protocol it uses to read and write the remote.</p>
      <div class=3D"legend">
        <span><span class=3D"chip ok">Verified</span> seen in binaries, fil=
es or the live system</span>
        <span><span class=3D"chip inf">Inferred</span> deduced from names a=
nd structure, not yet confirmed</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section id=3D"glance">
      <h2>At a glance</h2>
      <div class=3D"facts">
        <div class=3D"fact"><span class=3D"k">Remote on USB</span><span cla=
ss=3D"v ir">046D:C122</span></div>
        <div class=3D"fact"><span class=3D"k">Remote family</span><span cla=
ss=3D"v">"Molson" (arch 14/16)</span></div>
        <div class=3D"fact"><span class=3D"k">App version</span><span class=
=3D"v">1.0.1.308</span></div>
        <div class=3D"fact"><span class=3D"k">Browser engine</span><span cl=
ass=3D"v">CEF 3.1547 / Chrome 29</span></div>
        <div class=3D"fact"><span class=3D"k">App runtime</span><span class=
=3D"v">Silverlight 5.1.20913</span></div>
        <div class=3D"fact"><span class=3D"k">Logic lives</span><span class=
=3D"v">setup.myharmony.com</span></div>
      </div>
      <p>The installed program is a browser shell plus a USB driver. Almost=
 all logic, including the UI, the sync engine and the protocol scripts, is =
downloaded from Logitech at runtime as Silverlight packages. Without Logite=
ch's servers the app cannot do anything.</p>
    </section>

    <section id=3D"stack">
      <h2>Layer stack</h2>
      <p class=3D"sub">From the launcher you double-click down to the HID r=
eports on the wire.</p>
