    <section id=3D"app">
      <h2>Silverlight app ("MartiniWeb")</h2>
      <p class=3D"sub">The app is split into packages that load on demand. =
These were in the local cache.</p>
      <div class=3D"tbl"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Package</th><th>What it does</th><th>Notable assembl=
ies</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>BootStrapper</code></td><td>First package loaded. D=
ownloads the rest.</td><td class=3D"ops">Web.MartiniWeb.Downloader</td></tr=
>
          <tr><td><code>Core</code></td><td>Shell, dependency injection, da=
ta access, protocol driver.</td><td class=3D"ops">Web.Driver, Engine.Remote=
Communicator, Data.HarmonyPlatform, Data.DesktopServices, Data.RestPlatform=
, Prism, Ninject</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Account.Login</code></td><td>Sign in, create accoun=
t.</td><td class=3D"ops">Data.HarmonyPlatform</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Account.Management</code></td><td>Account settings.=
</td><td class=3D"ops">=E2=80=94</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Dashboard.Main</code></td><td>Home screen: devices,=
 activities, remote.</td><td class=3D"ops">ButtonMapping, ButtonMappingUtil=
s</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Device.AddDevice</code></td><td>Search and add a TV=
, AV receiver and so on.</td><td class=3D"ops">Driver, RemoteCommunicator, =
Activity.Setup</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Activity.Setup</code></td><td>Build activities like=
 "Watch TV".</td><td class=3D"ops">RemoteSync, ButtonMapping</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>ActivityRemote.ButtonMapping</code></td><td>Customi=
ze buttons per activity or device.</td><td class=3D"ops">ButtonMappingUtils=
</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>Remote.RemoteSync</code></td><td>The sync screen an=
d progress.</td><td class=3D"ops">=E2=80=94</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <h3>JavaScript bridge</h3>
      <p>The page creates the USB plugin as <code>&lt;object id=3D"HarmonyP=
lugin" type=3D"application/x-harmonyplugin"&gt;</code> and stores it in the=
 global <code>remoteEngine</code>. The Silverlight driver calls it through =
the browser bridge. It first checks for <code>window.jsHandler</code>. In t=
his shell, <code>jsHandler</code> only offers <code>clearCache</code>, <cod=
e>getAppVersion</code>, <code>getKeyBoardLocale</code>, <code>getKeyboardLa=
yout</code> and <code>silverlightLoaded</code>, so all device I/O goes to t=
he plugin. <span class=3D"chip ok">Verified</span></p>
      <p><code>HarmonyConfig.js</code> also contains a WebSocket client tha=
t sends <code>hbus</code> commands to a Harmony Hub through the cloud. It i=
s not used with a 600.</p>
    </section>

