      <p class=3D"caption">The order and the device-side commands match the=
 templates. Exactly which call returns the config binary is <span class=3D"=
chip inf">Inferred</span> and should be confirmed by watching a sync.</p>
      <h3>Learning IR</h3>
      <p>The reverse path: put the remote in learning mode, open <code>/ir/=
ir_cap</code>, read the captured signal, send it to <code>IInfraredAnalysis=
Manager.AnalyzeInfrared</code>, then save the result as a device command. <=
span class=3D"chip inf">Inferred</span> for the cloud step.</p>
    </section>

    <section id=3D"risks">
      <h2>Risks</h2>
      <div class=3D"callout risk">
        <p><span class=3D"chip risk">Cloud dependency</span></p>
        <p>The app has no offline mode. If <code>setup.myharmony.com</code>=
 or <code>files.myharmony.com</code> goes away, the remote can no longer be=
 reconfigured with this software.</p>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"callout risk">
        <p><span class=3D"chip risk">Old runtime</span></p>
        <p>Chrome 29 from 2013 runs with the sandbox off and loads remote c=
ode, alongside Silverlight 5, which Microsoft no longer supports. Run the a=
pp only while you need it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"callout risk">
        <p><span class=3D"chip risk">Open debug port</span></p>
        <p>The DevTools port <code>127.0.0.1:8088</code> needs no password.=
 Any program on the PC could control the signed-in session while the app is=
 open.</p>
      </div>
      <p class=3D"caption">The <code>$ is not defined</code> lines in <code=
>console.log</code> are harmless. <code>InstallSoftware.js</code> loads bef=
ore jQuery.</p>
    </section>

    <section id=3D"evidence">
      <h2>Evidence</h2>
      <p class=3D"sub">Where each finding came from. The extracted copies a=
re in a temporary session folder and should be moved into the repo before i=
t is cleaned up.</p>
      <div class=3D"tbl"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Location</th><th>What it showed</th><=
/tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Install folder</td><td><code>C:\Program Files (x86)\Logit=
ech\MyHarmony</code></td><td>Launcher, CEF shell, plugins, bundled Silverli=
ght</td></tr>
          <tr><td>HTTP cache</td><td><code>AppFiles\temp\data\f_*</code></t=
d><td>Host page HTML and 9 unique XAP packages</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Extracted XAPs</td><td>session folder <code>x\</code></td=
><td>Assemblies and service contracts</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Device table</td><td>session folder <code>rom\r334.xml</c=
ode></td><td>VID/PID =E2=86=92 model =E2=86=92 templates</td></tr>
          <tr><td>ROM templates</td><td>session folder <code>rom\r*.xml</co=
de></td><td>Protocol steps per remote family</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Page scripts</td><td>session folder <code>js\</code></td>=
<td>Plugin init and Hub WebSocket client</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Helper scripts</td><td>session folder <code>tools\</code>=
</td><td><code>xap.py</code>, <code>ext.py</code>, <code>str.py</code>, <co=
de>cdp.mjs</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Live system</td><td>process list, TCP table, PnP devices<=
/td><td>Process tree, endpoints, remote on USB</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
    </section>

    <section id=3D"next">
      <h2>Open threads</h2>
      <p class=3D"sub">Where to pick up next time, roughly in order.</p>
      <ol class=3D"threads">
        <li><b>Move the extracted material into the repo</b><span>Copy the =
XAPs, templates, scripts and tools out of the temporary session folder.</sp=
an></li>
        <li><b>Restart MyHarmony to free the DevTools slot</b><span>The fir=
st probe left Chrome 29's single debugger slot taken. After a restart, conn=
ect once with the raw client in <code>cdp.mjs</code>.</span></li>
        <li><b>Record a real sync</b><span>Capture network and console traf=
fic during one sync to confirm which call returns the config binary and fil=
l in the inferred steps.</span></li>
        <li><b>Decompile the driver</b><span>Open <code>Web.Driver.dll</cod=
e> and <code>RemoteSync.dll</code> in ILSpy to confirm how templates are ch=
osen and how <code>performOperation</code> results are parsed.</span></li>
        <li><b>Identify the exact model</b><span>Run only the read steps of=
 <code>identifyremote</code> to learn whether the 600 reports model 66 or 9=
6, plus its skin and firmware.</span></li>
        <li><b>Offline backup</b><span>The templates include a read path fo=
r the user configuration. A read-only backup tool would protect the setup i=
f Logitech's servers shut down.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <footer>Prepared with Claude from a read-only analysis of the running a=
pp. Nothing was written to the remote.</footer>
  </main>
